issue.body:
### Describe the situation
MergeTree stores a mostly-empty String column as Sparse. Expanding it for GROUP BY, JOIN or most functions uses the generic `IColumn::createWithOffsets`: one virtual insert per value and per run of empty strings. A String version that allocates once and copies all values together removes this cost.

Hot query time, ms: 6 paired rounds (median of 5 runs each), 95% CI. ClickBench hits, x86-64 4 vCPU; MobilePhoneModel is Sparse.

| Query | master | patched | Change [95% CI] |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| S2: `SELECT MobilePhoneModel, count() FROM hits WHERE MobilePhoneModel <> '' GROUP BY MobilePhoneModel ORDER BY count() DESC, MobilePhoneModel LIMIT 10` | 108 | 93 | −13.8% [−14.4%, −13.1%] |
| S4: `SELECT max(length(MobilePhoneModel \|\| 'x')) FROM hits` | 185.5 | 160 | −14.3% [−15.5%, −13.0%] |
| S1: `SELECT MobilePhoneModel, count() FROM hits GROUP BY MobilePhoneModel ORDER BY count() DESC, MobilePhoneModel LIMIT 10` | 178.5 | 160.5 | −9.7% [−11.8%, −7.6%] |
| Q10 (ClickBench `MobilePhoneModel, COUNT(DISTINCT UserID)`) | 306.5 | 293.5 | −4.3% [−5.0%, −3.7%] |
| Q11 (ClickBench `MobilePhone, MobilePhoneModel, COUNT(DISTINCT UserID)`) | 377.5 | 365.5 | −3.4% [−4.1%, −2.7%] |
| S5: `GROUP BY UTMSource, UTMMedium` (both Sparse, almost no values) | 972 | 959.5 | −1.3% [−1.8%, −0.9%] |
| Control Q12 (SearchPhrase, not Sparse) | 1178.5 | 1175.5 | −0.2% [−0.8%, +0.3%] |
| Control Q7 (AdvEngineID, numeric Sparse) | 18 | 18 | −0.1% [−3.7%, +3.7%] |
| `max_threads = 1`: S2 / S4 / S1 / Q10 | 193.5 / 367.5 / 408.5 / 708 | 171 / 315 / 369 / 685.5 | −12.2% / −14.0% / −9.4% / −3.9% |
| Cold (caches dropped, restart), median of 4: S2 / S1 / Q10 | 208.5 / 266 / 632.5 | 197.5 / 248.5 / 627.5 | −5% / −7% / −1% |
| 4 clients, 3 × (S2, Q10) each, wall time | 5.70 s | 5.38 s | −5.6% |
| `INSERT INTO t (s String, never Sparse) SELECT MobilePhoneModel FROM hits` | 724.5 | 673 | −7% (stored data identical) |

Peak memory is unchanged (Q10: 70.9 vs 70.7 MiB). Only String columns change; numeric Sparse columns already have their own `createWithOffsets`.

<details><summary>Why it happens and what the patch changes</summary>

A column is written Sparse when at least 93.75% of its values are default (`ratio_of_defaults_for_sparse_serialization`). In ClickBench, `MobilePhoneModel` (94.4% empty) and the `UTM*` columns are Sparse. When a consumer needs a full column, `ColumnSparse::convertToFullColumnIfSparse` calls `values->createWithOffsets(...)`, and the sparse path of `IFunction` builds a function's result the same way.

`ColumnVector` and `ColumnNullable` override `createWithOffsets`, but `ColumnString` does not, so `IColumn::createWithOffsets` inserts every value with a virtual `insertFrom` and every run of defaults with a virtual `insertManyFrom`, growing the result as it goes. In `perf` on master 358b8300 this is 5.4% of Q10's CPU, 19.6% of S1's and 46.5% of S4's (S4 materializes `'x'` for every empty row).

The patch adds a String path to `IColumn::createWithOffsets`: it sizes the result once and writes the offsets in one pass. When the default is empty (always the case for a Sparse column), the bytes of all values are copied with one `memcpy`. Otherwise (a function result such as `s || 'x'`), each default and value is copied with `memcpySmallAllowReadWriteOverflow15`, as `ColumnString::insertManyFrom` does. It also checks that the offsets increase and fit into the result.

Correctness: every warmup and timed response of every query above was kept and was identical on both builds. A targeted script (Sparse String tables with values, all defaults, values in the first and last rows; full reads, `GROUP BY`, `||` and `concat` with a non-empty default, `if`, `upper`, `toNullable`, `JOIN`, `ORDER BY`) gives identical output, and 80 `0_stateless/*sparse*` tests give identical output on both builds.

</details>

### Which ClickHouse versions are affected?
<details><summary>Tested versions and source commits</summary>

Measured with local Release builds (clang-21, no ThinLTO) of master 80e33a63b37bde382fbab0dbf3dac21a48402b4e (2026-11-03) without and with the patch, built in the same build directory. `IColumn::createWithOffsets`, `ColumnString`, `ColumnSparse` and the sparse path of `IFunction` are unchanged on master 83189467697c250c364a631283c302600de78eb5 (2026-11-06). The profile shares above are from the official master build 358b8300e8bb.

</details>

### How to reproduce
<details><summary>Data, queries and measurement procedure</summary>

Load ClickBench `hits` with its `create.sql` and check which columns are Sparse:

```sql
SELECT column, serialization_kind, count() FROM system.parts_columns
WHERE active AND table = 'hits' AND serialization_kind = 'Sparse' GROUP BY ALL;
```

Queries (besides S1, S2 and S4 in the table):

```sql
-- Q10
SELECT MobilePhoneModel, COUNT(DISTINCT UserID) AS u FROM hits WHERE MobilePhoneModel <> '' GROUP BY MobilePhoneModel ORDER BY u DESC LIMIT 10;
-- Q11
SELECT MobilePhone, MobilePhoneModel, COUNT(DISTINCT UserID) AS u FROM hits WHERE MobilePhoneModel <> '' GROUP BY MobilePhone, MobilePhoneModel ORDER BY u DESC LIMIT 10;
-- S5
SELECT UTMSource, UTMMedium, count() FROM hits GROUP BY UTMSource, UTMMedium ORDER BY count() DESC, UTMSource, UTMMedium LIMIT 10;
-- Q12, Q7 (controls)
SELECT SearchPhrase, COUNT(*) AS c FROM hits WHERE SearchPhrase <> '' GROUP BY SearchPhrase ORDER BY c DESC, SearchPhrase LIMIT 10;
SELECT AdvEngineID, COUNT(*) FROM hits WHERE AdvEngineID <> 0 GROUP BY AdvEngineID ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC;
```

The table had 2 Wide parts (ZSTD(3)), merges stopped. Each of 6 rounds started a fresh server per build in ABBA order and ran every query once as warmup and 5 times timed; the statistic is the per-round median of `query_duration_ms` from `system.query_log`, and the interval is a Student-t 95% interval of the paired log ratio. Default settings (4 threads on this host).

</details>

### Expected performance
<details><summary>Expected behavior</summary>

Expanding a Sparse String column should cost about one copy of its values plus one pass over the offsets, as it already does for numeric columns, instead of a virtual call per value and per run of defaults.

</details>

### Additional context
<details><summary>Full patch</summary>

```diff
diff --git a/src/Columns/IColumn.cpp b/src/Columns/IColumn.cpp
index f0eda7bf76c..3a534665b3f 100644
--- a/src/Columns/IColumn.cpp
+++ b/src/Columns/IColumn.cpp
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 #include <base/types.h>
 #include <Common/Exception.h>
 #include <Common/SipHash.h>
+#include <Common/memcpySmall.h>

 using Hash = CityHash_v1_0_2::uint128;
 using HashState = SipHash;
@@ -107,6 +108,101 @@ void IColumn::updateHashWithValueRange(size_t begin, size_t end, SipHash & hash)
         updateHashWithValue(i, hash);
 }

+namespace
+{
+
+/// `createWithOffsets` for `String`. The generic implementation inserts every value and every run of defaults through
+/// a virtual call, which is most of the cost of turning a sparse `String` column into a full one. Here the result is
+/// allocated once and its offsets are written in one pass; when the default is empty (always for a sparse column) the
+/// bytes of all values are copied at once. The chars of `ColumnString` are padded, so short copies may overrun by 15 bytes.
+ColumnPtr createStringWithOffsets(
+    const ColumnString & values, const IColumn::Offsets & offsets, const ColumnString & default_value, size_t total_rows, size_t shift)
+{
+    const size_t num_values = offsets.size();
+    if (num_values > total_rows || (num_values != 0 && offsets.back() >= total_rows))
+        throw Exception(
+            ErrorCodes::LOGICAL_ERROR,
+            "Offsets ({} values, last {}) do not fit into {} rows",
+            num_values,
+            num_values ? offsets.back() : 0,
+            total_rows);
+
+    const auto & values_offsets = values.getOffsets();
+    const auto & values_chars = values.getChars();
+    const size_t values_begin = values_offsets[static_cast<ssize_t>(shift) - 1];
+    const size_t values_bytes = values_chars.size() - values_begin;
+
+    const auto & default_offsets = default_value.getOffsets();
+    const size_t default_size = default_offsets[0] - default_offsets[-1];
+    const UInt8 * default_data = default_value.getChars().data() + default_offsets[-1];
+
+    auto res = ColumnString::create();
+    auto & res_chars = res->getChars();
+    auto & res_offsets = res->getOffsets();
+    res_chars.resize(values_bytes + default_size * (total_rows - num_values));
+    res_offsets.resize(total_rows);
+
+    UInt8 * chars_out = res_chars.data();
+    IColumn::Offset * offsets_out = res_offsets.data();
+    size_t row = 0;
+    size_t written = 0;
+
+    auto check_order = [&](size_t value_row)
+    {
+        if (value_row < row) [[unlikely]]
+            throw Exception(ErrorCodes::LOGICAL_ERROR, "Offsets of non-default values are not increasing ({} after {})", value_row, row - 1);
+    };
+
+    if (default_size == 0)
+    {
+        if (values_bytes)
+            memcpy(chars_out, values_chars.data() + values_begin, values_bytes);
+
+        for (size_t i = 0; i < num_values; ++i)
+        {
+            const size_t value_row = offsets[i];
+            check_order(value_row);
+            std::fill(offsets_out + row, offsets_out + value_row, written);
+            written = values_offsets[i + shift] - values_begin;
+            offsets_out[value_row] = written;
+            row = value_row + 1;
+        }
+        std::fill(offsets_out + row, offsets_out + total_rows, written);
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        auto insert_defaults = [&](size_t end)
+        {
+            for (; row < end; ++row)
+            {
+                memcpySmallAllowReadWriteOverflow15(chars_out + written, default_data, default_size);
+                written += default_size;
+                offsets_out[row] = written;
+            }
+        };
+
+        for (size_t i = 0; i < num_values; ++i)
+        {
+            const size_t value_row = offsets[i];
+            check_order(value_row);
+            insert_defaults(value_row);
+            const size_t value_begin = values_offsets[static_cast<ssize_t>(i + shift) - 1];
+            const size_t value_size = values_offsets[i + shift] - value_begin;
+            memcpySmallAllowReadWriteOverflow15(chars_out + written, values_chars.data() + value_begin, value_size);
+            written += value_size;
+            offsets_out[value_row] = written;
+            row = value_row + 1;
+        }
+        insert_defaults(total_rows);
+    }
+
+    chassert(written == res_chars.size());
+    return res;
+}
+
+}
+
+
 ColumnPtr IColumn::createWithOffsets(const Offsets & offsets, const ColumnConst & column_with_default_value, size_t total_rows, size_t shift) const
 {
     if (offsets.size() + shift != size())
@@ -117,6 +213,10 @@ ColumnPtr IColumn::createWithOffsets(const Offsets & offsets, const ColumnConst
             shift,
             size());

+    if (const auto * column_string = typeid_cast<const ColumnString *>(this))
+        if (const auto * default_string = typeid_cast<const ColumnString *>(&column_with_default_value.getDataColumn()))
+            return createStringWithOffsets(*column_string, offsets, *default_string, total_rows, shift);
+
     auto res = cloneEmpty();
     res->reserve(total_rows);

```

@groeneai could you take a look? If the analysis and patch hold up, feel free to open a PR if it fits.

</details>


