issue.body:
### Describe the situation
A `WHERE` condition that keeps exactly the non-default rows of a Sparse column (`s != ''`, `x != 0`) is applied by `ColumnSparse::index`, which copies each kept value with a virtual `insertFrom`. The patch shares the values column in that case and otherwise copies runs of consecutive values at once.

Hot query time, ms: 5 paired rounds (median of 5 runs each), 95% CI. ClickBench hits, x86-64 4 vCPU, default settings.

| Query | master | patched | Change [95% CI] |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| S2: `SELECT MobilePhoneModel, count() FROM hits WHERE MobilePhoneModel <> '' GROUP BY MobilePhoneModel ORDER BY count() DESC, MobilePhoneModel LIMIT 10` | 107 | 77 | −28.3% [−29.7%, −27.0%] |
| ClickBench Q7: `SELECT AdvEngineID, COUNT(*) FROM hits WHERE AdvEngineID <> 0 GROUP BY AdvEngineID ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC` | 18 | 15 | −14.7% [−18.0%, −11.4%] |
| S7: `SELECT UTMSource, count() FROM hits WHERE UTMSource <> '' GROUP BY UTMSource ORDER BY count() DESC, UTMSource LIMIT 10` | 46 | 37 | −17.1% [−25.0%, −8.4%] |
| S9: S2 also grouped by `UTMSource`, `SETTINGS optimize_move_to_prewhere = 0` (another Sparse column kept by the same filter) | 171 | 146 | −19.9% [−32.2%, −5.3%] |
| `sparse_column_index_sorted.xml` (200M rows): `SELECT a, count() ... WHERE a != 0 GROUP BY a` / `SELECT sum(b) ... WHERE a != 0` | 77 / 250 | 63.5 / 249 | −17.9% [−25.6%, −9.5%] / −0.7% [−4.3%, +3.1%] |
| `sparse_column_filter.xml` table with 10% non-empty `str` (50M rows): `SELECT str, count() ... WHERE notEmpty(str) GROUP BY str` | 503.5 | 472.5 | −6.6% [−8.1%, −5.1%] |
| `sparse_column_index_runs.xml`, run length 1 / 64 | 199 / 38.5 | 200.5 / 35 | +0.6% [−0.6%, +1.8%] / −9.0% [−15.2%, −2.3%] |
| Not this path (`PREWHERE` or no filter): Q10 / Q11 / S1 `GROUP BY MobilePhoneModel` / S5 `GROUP BY UTMSource, UTMMedium` / Q12 | 309 / 381 / 179 / 972 / 1181 | 307 / 379 / 178 / 972 / 1180 | −0.5% / −0.6% / 0.0% / −0.2% / −0.1%, every CI includes 0 |
| `max_threads = 1`, median of 4 rounds: S2 / S7 / Q7 / S9 | 196.5 / 83 / 30.5 / 327.5 | 147 / 66 / 25 / 274.5 | −25% / −20% / −18% / −16% |
| 4 clients, 3 × (S2, S7, Q7, S9) each, wall time, median of 4 rounds | 5.37 s | 4.59 s | −14.5% |
| `INSERT INTO t SELECT MobilePhoneModel FROM hits WHERE MobilePhoneModel <> ''`, median of 4 | 218 | 179.5 | −18% (stored data identical) |
| Cold (caches dropped, restart), median of 4: S2 / Q7 | 1539 / 1324 | 1532 / 1290 | no difference beyond I/O noise |

Peak memory is unchanged (S2: 1 MiB on both builds).

<details><summary>Why it happens and what the patch changes</summary>

When a condition is non-zero for every non-default value of a Sparse column and zero for the default, `IFunction` returns it as `Sparse(UInt8)` with the column's own offsets. `FilterTransform` then applies it with `SparseFilterDescription`, which calls `IColumn::index` with those offsets on every column of the block. This happens whenever the condition stays in `WHERE`, for example when the filtered column is the only column the query reads (S2, S7, Q7), or with `optimize_move_to_prewhere = 0` (S9).

For the column the condition came from, the indexes are exactly its offsets. `ColumnSparse::indexImpl` finds each of them with the galloping search of #126274, then inserts every value with a virtual `insertFrom` (for `String`, the chars also grow one value at a time) and pushes one offset. Runs of repeated indexes already use `insertManyFrom` (#118237), but a filter never repeats an index.

The patch changes `ColumnSparse::indexImpl` only:
- When the indexes equal the column's offsets, the result shares `values` and its offsets are 0 .. n-1, so nothing is copied.
- Otherwise, single rows whose values are consecutive in `values` are collected and copied with one `insertRangeFrom`; a run of one value still uses `insertFrom`, and repeated indexes still use `insertManyFrom`.

Correctness: every warm-up and timed response of every query above was kept and is identical on both builds. A script with Sparse and non-Sparse copies of the same data (3 parts; `String`, numeric and `Nullable` columns; filters on the same and on other Sparse columns, `optimize_move_to_prewhere = 0`, small `max_block_size`, primary-key ranges, `JOIN` with repeated rows, `ORDER BY`) gives identical results on both builds. Sparse and non-Sparse tables also agree, except for one `groupArray` order difference that master has as well (#123817). 92 `0_stateless/*sparse*` tests give identical output on both builds.

</details>

### Which ClickHouse versions are affected?
<details><summary>Tested versions and source commits</summary>

Measured with local Release builds (clang-21, no ThinLTO) of master 80e33a63b37bde382fbab0dbf3dac21a48402b4e (2026-11-03) without and with the patch, built in the same build directory. `ColumnSparse`, `IColumn`, `ColumnString`, `ColumnVector` and the sparse path of `IFunction` are unchanged on master c9e18d01727ebb09cb9e06ee90a4b436d5a3fb3a (2026-11-06); `FilterTransform.cpp` and `FilterDescription.cpp` changed there only in unrelated code (memory-tracking containers, the in-place filter helper of #129188).

</details>

### How to reproduce
<details><summary>Data, queries and measurement procedure</summary>

Load ClickBench `hits` with its `create.sql` and check which columns are Sparse (here `AdvEngineID`, `MobilePhoneModel` and the `UTM*` columns):

```sql
SELECT column, serialization_kind, count() FROM system.parts_columns
WHERE active AND table = 'hits' AND serialization_kind = 'Sparse' GROUP BY ALL;
```

Queries not spelled out in the table:

```sql
-- S9
SELECT MobilePhoneModel, UTMSource, count() FROM hits WHERE MobilePhoneModel <> '' GROUP BY MobilePhoneModel, UTMSource ORDER BY count() DESC, MobilePhoneModel, UTMSource LIMIT 10 SETTINGS optimize_move_to_prewhere = 0;
-- S1, S5
SELECT MobilePhoneModel, count() FROM hits GROUP BY MobilePhoneModel ORDER BY count() DESC, MobilePhoneModel LIMIT 10;
SELECT UTMSource, UTMMedium, count() FROM hits GROUP BY UTMSource, UTMMedium ORDER BY count() DESC, UTMSource, UTMMedium LIMIT 10;
-- Q10, Q11, Q12
SELECT MobilePhoneModel, COUNT(DISTINCT UserID) AS u FROM hits WHERE MobilePhoneModel <> '' GROUP BY MobilePhoneModel ORDER BY u DESC, MobilePhoneModel LIMIT 10;
SELECT MobilePhone, MobilePhoneModel, COUNT(DISTINCT UserID) AS u FROM hits WHERE MobilePhoneModel <> '' GROUP BY MobilePhone, MobilePhoneModel ORDER BY u DESC, MobilePhone, MobilePhoneModel LIMIT 10;
SELECT SearchPhrase, COUNT(*) AS c FROM hits WHERE SearchPhrase <> '' GROUP BY SearchPhrase ORDER BY c DESC, SearchPhrase LIMIT 10;
```

The performance-test rows use the tables of `tests/performance/sparse_column_index_sorted.xml` (200M rows instead of 500M), `sparse_column_index_runs.xml` and `sparse_column_filter.xml` (`ratio` 10, 50M rows), with their queries and settings.

The `hits` table had 2 Wide parts (ZSTD(3)), merges stopped. Each of 5 rounds started a fresh server per build in rotating order and ran every query once as warm-up and 5 times timed; the statistic is the per-round median of `query_duration_ms` from `system.query_log`, and the interval is a Student-t 95% interval of the paired log ratio (4 rounds of 3 timed runs for the performance-test rows). Default settings (4 threads on this host).

</details>

### Expected performance
<details><summary>Expected behavior</summary>

Applying a Sparse filter to the column it was computed from should cost almost nothing, because the kept rows are exactly the stored values; keeping a subset of another Sparse column should cost one copy per run of consecutive values, not one virtual call per row.

</details>

### Related issues and pull requests
<details><summary>Related work</summary>

- https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/issues/129680 (the same one-value-at-a-time copy in `IColumn::createWithOffsets` for Sparse `String`; independent of this patch)
- https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/pull/126274
- https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/pull/128852 (open; changes how the linear path of `indexImpl` fills `values_index`, independent of this patch)
- https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/pull/118237
- https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/pull/128396
- https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/issues/123817

</details>

### Additional context
<details><summary>Full patch</summary>

@groeneai could you take a look? If the analysis and patch hold up, feel free to open a PR if it fits.

```diff
