<details><summary>Why it happens and what the patch changes</summary>

When a condition is non-zero for every non-default value of a Sparse column and zero for the default, `IFunction` returns it as `Sparse(UInt8)` with the column's own offsets. `FilterTransform` then applies it with `SparseFilterDescription`, which calls `IColumn::index` with those offsets on every column of the block. This happens whenever the condition stays in `WHERE`, for example when the filtered column is the only column the query reads (S2, S7, Q7), or with `optimize_move_to_prewhere = 0` (S9).

